ing for  me  I love this great quote from you if I'm  going to cook I'm going to cook food  that takes you out at your knees yeah  Wow thank you yeah you know it's a it's  a philosophy that we definitely hold  true at the Beatrice because what we  always say is that you know everything  great starts around the dinner table  this is a restaurant that has like an  80-year history right but but when they  approached you and not always a great  history but right when they approached  you about being an executive chef  initially you were I didn't want it you  do you know I was working at a really  great restaurant at the time and it's  such a tumultuous history but I wasn't  really sure that I wanted to do that and  I haven't really made my name for myself  yet I was just kind of finding my way  and I called a very good friend of mine  Pat LaFrieda who is one of America's  biggest butchers yes we've profiled on  the show yeah he's fantastic and you  know I I called him and I said you know  look they want me to take this job and I  think it might be career suicide and he  said you know what it could be but it if  you turn it around it's gonna make your  career Wow Wow  so you not only did you turn it around  in three short years you went from being  head chef to head honcho own the  beatrice thinness yeah I bought it two  years ago  yeah I have doubts about buying it too I  did I went back to Pat LaFrieda Pat and  I really but what do I do it was like  should I hide for lottery numbers all  right I know what was his advice this  time you know what he told me was  everybody thought you were crazy from  for taking the job so if you buy it  you're just doubling down on crazy so  you might as well do it if you sign the  dish you could have this meal with  anyone pastor present I mean aside from  the three of you I think those are our  you know my father uh you know he was  such a huge inspiration for all the food  and really the ethos of the restaurant  itself and what it's b